    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Question\n\nI tried using one of the snippets listed in the docs for custom surroundings, specifically this one at line 573: \r\n```lua\r\n  surround.setup({\r\n    custom_surroundings = {\r\n      -- Make `)` insert parts with spaces. `input` pattern stays the same.\r\n      [')'] = { output = { left = '( ', right = ' )' } },\r\n``` \r\nand I found that whatever `count1` was used for `sa`to repeat the left and right surroundings would remain the same after first use. \r\n\r\nFor example, inputting `2saiw)` would cause all subsequent `sa` commands to repeat the surroundings twice no matter the new `count1` used, or textobject. This would happen regardless of the new mapping, so subsituting `['f']` would cause the same behavior. I've also tested it with different outputs and the same thing occurs.\r\n```lua\r\n-- first command: 2saiw)\r\n( ( abc ) )\r\n-- second command: 10saiw)\r\n( ( abc ) )\r\n--third: saiw)\r\n( ( abc ) )\r\n```\r\n\r\n<details> <summary>config</summary>\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.pack.add({ 'https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim' })\r\nrequire('mini.surround').setup({\r\n\tcustom_surroundings = {\r\n\t\t[')'] = { output = { left = 'a', right = 'a' } }\r\n\t}\r\n})\r\n```\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nMaybe it's listed in the documentation and I haven't read it (sorry!), but any help and clarification on this greatly appreciated! and thank you to everybody for all your work on mini :)\r\n\r\n\r\n",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.surround</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I tried using one of the snippets listed in the docs for custom surroundings, specifically this one at line 573:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"  surround.setup({\n    custom_surroundings = {\n      -- Make `)` insert parts with spaces. `input` pattern stays the same.\n      [')'] = { output = { left = '( ', right = ' )' } },\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">  <span class=\"pl-smi\">surround</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">custom_surroundings</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n      <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Make `)` insert parts with spaces. `input` pattern stays the same.</span>\n      [<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>)<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>] <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-smi\">output</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-smi\">left</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>( <span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">right</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span> )<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>} },</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">and I found that whatever <code class=\"notranslate\">count1</code> was used for <code class=\"notranslate\">sa</code>to repeat the left and right surroundings would remain the same after first use.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For example, inputting <code class=\"notranslate\">2saiw)</code> would cause all subsequent <code class=\"notranslate\">sa</code> commands to repeat the surroundings twice no matter the new <code class=\"notranslate\">count1</code> used, or textobject. This would happen regardless of the new mapping, so subsituting <code class=\"notranslate\">['f']</code> would cause the same behavior. I've also tested it with different outputs and the same thing occurs.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"-- first command: 2saiw)\n( ( abc ) )\n-- second command: 10saiw)\n( ( abc ) )\n--third: saiw)\n( ( abc ) )\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> first command: 2saiw)</span>\n( ( <span class=\"pl-smi\">abc</span> ) )\n<span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> second command: 10saiw)</span>\n( ( <span class=\"pl-smi\">abc</span> ) )\n<span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span>third: saiw)</span>\n( ( <span class=\"pl-smi\">abc</span> ) )</pre></div>\n<details> <summary>config</summary>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.pack.add({ 'https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim' })\nrequire('mini.surround').setup({\n\tcustom_surroundings = {\n\t\t[')'] = { output = { left = 'a', right = 'a' } }\n\t}\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">pack</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">add</span>({ <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>})\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.surround<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n\t<span class=\"pl-smi\">custom_surroundings</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n\t\t[<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>)<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>] <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-smi\">output</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-smi\">left</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>a<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">right</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>a<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>} }\n\t}\n})</pre></div>\n</details>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Maybe it's listed in the documentation and I haven't read it (sorry!), but any help and clarification on this greatly appreciated! and thank you to everybody for all your work on mini :)</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.surround\nQuestion\nI tried using one of the snippets listed in the docs for custom surroundings, specifically this one at line 573:\n  surround.setup({\n    custom_surroundings = {\n      -- Make `)` insert parts with spaces. `input` pattern stays the same.\n      [')'] = { output = { left = '( ', right = ' )' } },\nand I found that whatever count1 was used for sato repeat the left and right surroundings would remain the same after first use.\nFor example, inputting 2saiw) would cause all subsequent sa commands to repeat the surroundings twice no matter the new count1 used, or textobject. This would happen regardless of the new mapping, so subsituting ['f'] would cause the same behavior. I've also tested it with different outputs and the same thing occurs.\n-- first command: 2saiw)\n( ( abc ) )\n-- second command: 10saiw)\n( ( abc ) )\n--third: saiw)\n( ( abc ) )\n config\nvim.pack.add({ 'https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim' })\nrequire('mini.surround').setup({\n\tcustom_surroundings = {\n\t\t[')'] = { output = { left = 'a', right = 'a' } }\n\t}\n})\n\nMaybe it's listed in the documentation and I haven't read it (sorry!), but any help and clarification on this greatly appreciated! and thank you to everybody for all your work on mini :)",
